      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given an arithmetic sequence that has ${a}_{10}=23$ and the common difference $d=3$, what is the general formula for the $n$th term of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "Since ${a}_{10}=23$ is $9$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{10} & ={a}_{1}+9d \\\\ 23 & ={a}_{1}+9(3) \\\\ 23 & ={a}_{1}+27 \\\\ -4 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)(3) \\\\  & =-4+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n-7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
